WEBVTT

NOTE Timing is estimated from script and acoustic pauses; listening review pending.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.170
It is Friday at 10:12 in the morning.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.467
Valentina has checked the supplier
message, the shipment sheet, the

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:16.115
campaign calendar, and the waitlist.

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:20.775
She sends the founder a long
update with every detail she found.

00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:25.435
The reply arrives one minute later:
“What do you need me to decide?”

00:00:25.435 --> 00:00:29.055
Nothing in Valentina’s
update was false.

00:00:29.055 --> 00:00:32.130
The problem was not accuracy.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.565
The problem was structure.

00:00:34.565 --> 00:00:39.387
She described her investigation in the
order she performed it and left the

00:00:39.387 --> 00:00:43.332
hardest work to the reader: finding
the conclusion, understanding the

00:00:43.332 --> 00:00:45.305
impact, and deciding what to do.

00:00:45.305 --> 00:00:50.774
At BonnaMira, useful
communication does more

00:00:50.774 --> 00:00:55.000
than report activity. It
helps the next person act.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.733
During this course, you will help
Valentina repair the message using

00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:04.230
DECIDE—a six-question planning
method that turns information into

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:04.940
direction.
